writetourl error writes xml like macos

-[NSDictionary writeToURL:error:] and the NSArray twin wrote a BINARY plist. macOS writes XML, and
the testsuite is the arbiter: its expected resource was captured from a real Mac and begins
"<plist version=" rather than "bplist00". The two NSDictionary writeToURL cases aborted because the
comparison read the generated file as empty.

The comment that justified binary is corrected in place rather than deleted, because the reasoning
in it (reading sniffs the format, so only the bytes on disk differ) is right and only the conclusion
was wrong.

Measured with scripts/run-dts-batch.sh: 35 passing to 37, exactly the two cases either way.

